# Accepted risks — TEMPORARY. Remove when a pip release vendors setuptools >= 78.1.1.
#
# All findings are pip's OWN vendored copies, not application dependencies.
# pip 26.2 (2026-07-29) began shipping a CycloneDX SBOM of its vendored libs
# (pip/_vendor/bom.cdx.json); trivy ingests in-image SBOMs, so these internal
# copies became visible to the scan even though nothing in this project
# installs or imports them. Verified 2026-08-03: a bare `python:3.12-slim`
# image with only `pip install --upgrade pip` reproduced exactly the msgpack
# and setuptools findings.

# setuptools 70.3.0: pip vendors only the pkg_resources subpackage — the
# vulnerable PackageIndex/easy_install code path is not shipped in the image.
# pip 26.3, the newest pip on 2026-11-02, still pins setuptools==70.3.0 in
# pip/_vendor/vendor.txt. Its msgpack 1.2.4 and urllib3 2.8.0 are fixed, so
# those entries were removed that day.
CVE-2025-47273
